# SAP骨架与ADaM数据集设计

## SAP Statistical Analysis Plan

---

## 1. SAP骨架目录

### 1. Title Page
- Study title
- Version
- Date
- Authors
- Participating centers

### 2. Introduction
- Clinical background
- Study rationale
- Why cavernous sinus–invading acromegaly is a distinct subgroup
- Role of GKS in multimodal management

### 3. Objectives

#### 3.1 Primary Objectives
- Durable endocrine remission
- Predictors of remission

#### 3.2 Secondary Objectives
- Radiographic control
- Recurrence
- Salvage treatment
- Hypopituitarism
- Toxicity

#### 3.3 Exploratory Objectives
- Early vs late remission
- Medication hold
- BED / dosimetry
- Dynamic prediction model

### 4. Study Design
- International multicenter retrospective cohort
- Index treatment definition
- Follow-up definition
- Analysis populations

### 5. Analysis Populations

#### 5.1 Full Analysis Set (FAS)
All eligible patients meeting inclusion/exclusion criteria.

#### 5.2 Endocrine Evaluable Set
Patients with baseline endocrine data and at least one post-GKS endocrine assessment.

#### 5.3 Imaging Evaluable Set
Patients with at least one post-GKS MRI assessment.

#### 5.4 Safety Set
All patients who underwent eligible index GKS and have post-treatment safety follow-up.

#### 5.5 Sensitivity Cohorts
- Postoperative residual-only
- Knosp 3–4 only
- Excluding primary GKS
- Targeted only / whole-sella only if needed

### 6. Study Definitions

#### 6.1 Index Date
First eligible GKS date.

#### 6.2 Baseline
Closest assessment before index GKS within predefined window.

#### 6.3 Endocrine Definitions
- Uncontrolled disease
- Endocrine control
- Biochemical remission
- Durable remission
- Biochemical recurrence

#### 6.4 Imaging Definitions
- Stable disease
- Regression
- Progression
- Tumor control

#### 6.5 Safety Definitions
- New hypopituitarism
- Visual toxicity
- Cranial neuropathy
- Radionecrosis / ARE

### 7. Endpoints

#### 7.1 Primary Endpoints
- Durable endocrine remission
- Time to endocrine remission
- Radiographic tumor control

#### 7.2 Secondary Endpoints
- Biochemical recurrence
- Salvage therapy
- New hypopituitarism
- Visual toxicity
- Cranial neuropathy
- OS

#### 7.3 Exploratory Endpoints
- 36-month early vs late remission
- 29-month sensitivity
- Medication-hold effect
- Dosimetric effect
- Predictive model performance

### 8. General Statistical Considerations
- Descriptive methods
- Significance level
- Confidence intervals
- Handling of continuous/categorical variables
- Multiplicity: exploratory, no formal adjustment unless specified
- Software: SAS / R / Python if ML arm included

### 9. Handling of Missing Data
- Missingness assessment
- Complete-case as sensitivity
- Multiple imputation strategy for covariates
- No imputation for event dates/status unless specifically adjudicated

### 10. Derivation Rules
- IGF-1i
- Baseline GH
- Baseline tumor volume
- Surgery-to-GKS interval
- Early vs delayed GKS
- Dose/BED strata
- Medication status categories

### 11. Statistical Methods

11.1 Descriptive statistics

11.2 Kaplan–Meier analyses

11.3 Cox regression

11.4 Logistic regression

11.5 Weighted / propensity-based comparisons

11.6 Sensitivity analyses

11.7 Exploratory ML analyses

### 12. Subgroup Analyses
- Knosp 1–2 vs 3–4
- Primary vs adjuvant GKS
- Targeted vs whole-sella
- Medication hold groups
- Low vs high IGF-1i
- Low vs high BED

### 13. Tables, Listings, Figures
- Planned TLF shells

### 14. Quality Control
- Data review
- Programming validation
- Endpoint adjudication

### 15. References

---

